# Focus Timings & Gear Icon Implementation

## Overview
The user wants to add presets for focus timings (which are already customizable) and move the "Customise Settings" button to a glassmorphic gear icon in the corner of the screen.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. [frontend/app/focus/page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/focus/page.tsx)
- **Move Customise Button**:
  - **[MODIFY]**: Remove the current "Customise Settings" button located below the Play and Reset timer buttons.
  - **[MODIFY]**: Add a new absolute-positioned button (e.g., `fixed` or `absolute top-6 right-6 z-30`) featuring a `Settings2` (or [Settings](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/focus/page.tsx#451-474)) gear icon from `lucide-react`. 
  - Style the new button with glassmorphic classes: `bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md border-[0.5px] border-white/20 text-white/80 hover:text-white hover:bg-white/20 rounded-full p-3 shadow-lg transition-all`.

- **Add Duration Presets**:
  - **[MODIFY]**: In the Customise Modal -> "Durations" tab (`customiseTab === 'durations'`), add a new "Presets" section above the manual number inputs.
  - The presets will be:
    - **Classic Pomodoro**: 25m Focus, 5m Short Break, 15m Long Break
    - **Deep Work**: 50m Focus, 10m Short Break, 30m Long Break
    - **Quick Burst**: 15m Focus, 3m Short Break, 10m Long Break
  - Clicking a preset will instantly update the `durationsForm` state so the user can see the numbers change before clicking "Save Durations".

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
Currently, there is no E2E test suite for the UI in Next.js. Validation will be performed manually or verified via compiler checks.
- Build the app to ensure no typing errors.

### Manual Verification
1. Navigate to [/focus](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/focus) in a browser.
2. Verify the old "Customise Settings" button is gone from the centre.
3. Verify the new glassmorphic gear icon is in the top-right corner.
4. Click the gear icon to open the modal.
5. Go to the "Durations" tab.
6. Click the "Deep Work" preset and ensure the inputs change to 50, 10, 30.
7. Click "Save Durations" and verify the timer limits are updated.
